// src/v4/extdeps/languages/typescript.dag
//
// Scope: TypeScript language model — direction-agnostic. Includes ES
//         (ECMAScript) base.
// Anchor: https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/everyday-types.html
//         (TypeScript Handbook) + https://tc39.es/ecma262/ (ECMAScript
//         specification) — the versioned upstream specifications (L-2
//         fidelity authority). The Handbook + ECMA-262 are the specs the
//         carriers below are pinned to; when the spec partition changes
//         (a new primitive; revised `Number` / `BigInt` semantics), the
//         change is a visible C1 edit to the relevant declaration below,
//         never a silent extension.
// Unifies: (per THESIS:188) language spec = transport spec = interpreter
//         runtime. ONE substrate carrier for all three roles. Different
//         lenses read different facts from the same data (emission reads
//         syntax; transport reads serialization; interpreter reads
//         execution semantics). A worker needing transport or runtime
//         extends this file, not a new "transport spec" file.
//
// Owns (this slice — T-4 typescript D2-resolver; **mirrors** the D2
//   resolver machine encoded in `extdeps/languages/rust.dag` at PR
//   #3174 / commit 0328bee95 + the operator-ratified DECISIONS.md D2
//   row, 2026-05-16 / PR #3195 merge 44a37ad46):
//
//   - TypeScript / ECMAScript primitive inhabitance as the D2a three-
//     thin-facts resolver: alias-identity to std/ carriers, grounding
//     map (surface spelling / keyword), operation-semantics siblings
//     (where the spec supplies a Rust-analogous disposition partition).
//   - The closed resolver-shape carriers `GroundingMap<IRCarrier>`,
//     `OverflowAction`, `OverflowDisposition<IRCarrier>` — **structural
//     parity** with the rust.dag D2 block so the generic B2-OMNI emit
//     fold (D2.2) reads one resolver vocabulary across Shape A targets.
//     **Semantic defaults are language-specific:** ECMAScript `number`
//     is IEEE-754 binary64 arithmetic (approximate field — see this
//     file's prior scaffold `number` → ApproximateField note); it does
//     NOT inherit Rust's debug `PanicOnOverflow` / release
//     `TwoComplementWrap` *defaults* for `+` on fixed-width integers.
//     Those two variants remain the **shared closed carrier** for any
//     future TS surface that genuinely maps to the same disposition
//     axis (e.g. Wasm strict i32 lowering, or a checked TypedArray
//     policy modeled explicitly). No `data ts_*_overflow` instance rows
//     are authored here for `boolean` or `number` — only types + the
//     landed `boolean` grounding row.
//   - TypeScript grammar (declarations, expressions, types, generics,
//     interfaces, classes), structural typing, and cost realization —
//     **preserved as goals** in the Owned ELSEWHERE table; this slice
//     lands D2 only (same slice-vs-bundled discipline as rust.dag
//     #3174 / ptx.dag #3170).
//
// Owned ELSEWHERE (named owners + dissolution triggers):
//
//   - Full bidirectional TypeScript `LanguageModel` (grammar as B2-OMNI
//     data, C5-fidelity disposition tags, ingest∘emit TestClaims) —
//     bundled T-4 Shape A work; rides ratified `Outcome<T>` when
//     std/diagnostic.dag lands (same STOP-triggers as rust.dag).
//   - Pipeline emit/ingest operations — compiler/05_emit.dag (T-10),
//     compiler/02_parse.dag (T-7); not language-file operations.
//   - Structural typing, excess property checks, conditional types —
//     C5-3 / B2-OMNI / B4; **D2 scope guard** (DECISIONS.md D2): D2
//     covers per-primitive inhabitance form ONLY — do not import D2
//     reasoning into those axes.
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/logic.dag: `Bool` (kernel-ambient; the D2a row `type TsBoolean
//     = Bool` references `Bool` without an import — same discipline as
//     rust.dag's `RustBool` row).
//   - `String` in `GroundingMap.spelling` is kernel-ambient boundary
//     text at the source-syntax edge (same as rust.dag's
//     `GroundingMap`).
//
// Status: T-4 typescript D2-resolver slice modeled 2026-05-16 — D2
//   machine mirrors rust #3174@0328bee95; bool alias-identity + grounding
//   landed; numeric / string / bigint / symbol rows 🟡 TRACKED-SCAFFOLD
//   per upstream std/ + refinement decisions (see resolver block).
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; this file's I/O contract is the immutable
// contract for the worker. Splitting this file requires explicit operator
// ratification (substrate extension = stop signal).


module v4.extdeps.languages.typescript


// Bool is KERNEL-AMBIENT (STRUCTURE.md). The D2a row `type TsBoolean =
// Bool` below references `Bool` directly; no `import` of std/logic.dag
// is required (rust.dag precedent).


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Modeling notes (D2 slice; read before extending)
//
// PRIMITIVE INHABITANCE (scaffold continuity — still binding intent):
//   - `number` → IEEE-754 binary64 `Float` / `ApproximateField` (NOT an
//     exact `Field`); same grounding as std/float.dag + std/algebra.dag.
//   - `string` → `FreeMonoid<Char>` via std/text.dag's `String` alias;
//     ECMA-262 `string` values are UTF-16 code unit sequences — a
//     **refinement** mismatch vs Unicode-scalar `Char` (mirrors rust.dag
//     char/str deferral until std/text refines or a disposition lands).
//   - `Array<T>` / `T[]` → `List<T>` (std/collection.dag) — compound;
//     D2.3 composes for free; no per-instantiation resolver rows.
// STRUCTURAL TYPING — Handbook structural rules are **out of D2** per
//   DECISIONS.md D2 scope guard; owned by C5-3 / B2-OMNI grammar work.


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// D2 RESOLVER SHAPE — per-primitive three-thin-facts declarations.
//
// Per the operator-ratified DECISIONS.md D2 row (2026-05-16, encoded via
// PR #3195 merge at 44a37ad46), a language extdeps file is a RESOLVER for
// the abstract std/ carriers. Per primitive, THREE thin declarations:
//
//   (1) alias-identity to the std/ carrier — algebra flows through the
//       alias (`List<T> = FreeMonoid<T>` precedent).
//   (2) grounding map (surface spelling / keyword).
//   (3) operation-semantics carriers — genuine per-language facts.
//
// Per D2.2: coercion = U1 homomorphism via the generic B2-OMNI emit fold
// reading resolver data — not a hand table, not a per-language emit lens.
//
// Per D2.3: compound / generic coercion composes via the Node catamorphism.
//
// Per D2.4: round-trip is structural-on-F per C5-1; TestClaims document.
//
// Per D2.5: overflow / UB / arbitrary-precision are DISTINCT std/ carriers
// selected by alias target + per-language disposition — never a re-
// declared parallel `OrderedRing<<lang>Prim, …>` inhabitance (INVARIANTS
// P1:42).
//
// Canonical rust encoding: `extdeps/languages/rust.dag` @ 0328bee95
// (PR #3174 reshape). This block mirrors that file's resolver carriers
// and the landed-bool pattern; deferral tables are TypeScript-specific.


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// GroundingMap<IRCarrier> — surface-spelling / keyword carrier (Conj).
//
// Per D2a(2). Each alias pairs with `data ts_*_grounding: GroundingMap<
// …> = GroundingMap { spelling: "<token>" }` at the source-syntax
// boundary (Handbook keyword or literal form), not in kernel code.
//
// Spec: https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-ecmascript-language-types
//       https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/2/everyday-types.html
type GroundingMap<IRCarrier> {
  spelling: String
}


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// OverflowAction — closed disposition partition carried in
// `OverflowDisposition` (D2a(3)).
//
// **Shared vocabulary with rust.dag** for the D2 resolver machine. Rust
// assigns these variants to fixed-width integer `+` defaults. TypeScript
// does not use that assignment for ECMAScript `number` (IEEE-754). Future
// rows that genuinely select among these variants must cite the spec edge
// they model (never silently reuse Rust defaults for `number`).
//
// Coproduct: 🟢 terminal for the **carrier shape**; ledger lives in
// rust.dag (PR #3174); not re-ledgered here — duplicate Practice-4 text
// would fork authority.
type OverflowAction
  = PanicOnOverflow
  | TwoComplementWrap


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// OverflowDisposition<IRCarrier> — per-target debug/release defaults
// for the overflow-action axis (Conj).
//
// Structural mirror of rust.dag. **No TsBoolean / TsNumber instance rows**
// here — `boolean` has no integer overflow; `number` is not a fixed-width
// int (IEEE-754 disposition lands with std/float.dag + float alias rows).
type OverflowDisposition<IRCarrier> {
  debug_default: OverflowAction
  release_default: OverflowAction
}


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Per-primitive alias-identity + grounding (LANDABLE NOW).

// ECMAScript / TypeScript `boolean` ↔ std/logic.dag `Bool`.
type TsBoolean = Bool

data ts_boolean_grounding: GroundingMap<TsBoolean> = GroundingMap {
  spelling: "boolean"
}

// No overflow disposition row for `boolean`.


// 🟡 TRACKED-SCAFFOLD — DEFERRED ALIAS-IDENTITY + SEMANTICS ROWS
//
// SUBSTRATE SINGLE-AUTHORITY GUARD (rust.dag #3174 precedent): this file
// MUST NOT mint std/ `Int` / `UInt` / `Float*` / `String` carriers
// locally — alias-identity to std/ only.
//
// ─── `number` (IEEE-754 binary64) — TsNumber = Float64
//   - grounding keyword        `"number"` (Handbook + TS grammar).
//   - operation semantics      NaN / ±Inf / rounding — D2b + std/float
//                              `ApproximateField` op `Arrow` bodies;
//                              NOT `OverflowDisposition` rows meant for
//                              Rust fixed-width ints.
//   - named owner              std/float.dag — Float32 / Float64 ladder.
//   - dissolution trigger      Float64 + ApproximateField inhabitance on
//                              origin/main in std/float.dag.
//
// ─── `bigint` — arbitrary-precision integer
//   - target form              alias to std/ arbitrary-precision `Int`
//                              (std/integer.dag) when that carrier is the
//                              ratified BigInt semantic target; ECMA-262
//                              throws on division-by-zero etc. — genuine
//                              per-spec facts, not Rust's wrap/panic axis.
//   - named owner              std/integer.dag (unbounded `Int` ladder).
//   - dissolution trigger      std/integer.dag lands BigInt-aligning alias
//                              target + explicit disposition table row.
//
// ─── `string` — TsString = String
//   - refinement tension       ECMA-262 `string` is UTF-16 code units;
//                              std/text `String = FreeMonoid<Char>` is
//                              Unicode-scalar-oriented — same class of
//                              deferral as rust.dag RustChar/RustStr.
//   - dissolution trigger      std/text refinement OR operator-ratified
//                              per-language disposition (rust.dag char/str
//                              table precedent).
//
// ─── `symbol` — ECMAScript `symbol` primitive
//   - deferral                 no stable std/ primitive alias yet; lands
//                              with kernel nominal/runtime carrier work
//                              or explicit "modeled as Node" disposition.
//
// ─── `null` / `undefined` — null types in TS type system
//   - deferral                 LanguageModel + strict-null checking live
//                              outside D2 primitive-inhabitance slice.


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// D2b — IEEE-754 `number` operation realizations.
//
// Per D2 row D2b: float primitives use `Transform → FunctionRef → Arrow`
// with `body` in extdeps/. Arrow-body source tokens / precedence live in
// the bundled T-4 TypeScript `LanguageModel` grammar — same deferral as
